\"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    # Each column has a fixed background value; diagonal cells are the\n    # previous value in the cycle, so exclude them when learning the pattern.\n    vals = []\n    for c in range(w):\n        counts = {}\n        for r in range(h):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v != 0 and r != c:\n                counts[v] = counts.get(v, 0) + 1\n        vals.append(max(counts, key=counts.get) if counts else None)\n\n    # Infer any entirely obscured columns from the repeating sequence.\n    known = [i for i, v in enumerate(vals) if v is not None]\n    for c in range(w):\n        if vals[c] is not None:\n            continue\n        candidates = []\n        for period in range(1, w + 1):\n            matches = sum(vals[i] is not None and\n                          vals[i] == vals[i % period]\n                          for i in known if i % period < len(vals))\n            if matches:\n                candidates.append((matches, -period, period))\n        if candidates:\n            period = max(candidates)[2]\n            vals[c] = vals[c % period]\n\n    # If the sequence could not be inferred from the columns, use the nearest\n    # available column's value.\n    for c in range(w):\n        if vals[c] is None:\n            vals[c] = next((vals[i] for i in range(w) if vals[i] is not None), 0)\n\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if out[r][c] == 0:\n                out[r][c] = vals[c - 1] if r == c and c > 0 else (\n                    vals[-1] if r == c else vals[c]\n                )\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":30,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793571152.982,"t1":1793571166.872,"alias":"task-20a42805","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n5 6 1 2 3 4 5 6 1 2 3 4 5 6 1 